// Worthy [CR#700.16]: a creature is worthy if it's legendary, isn't a Villain,
// and is red and/or white. A named compound predicate, not a new engine
// primitive — every piece already exists on `Predicate`. The `template` lets it
// render back to the bare adjective "worthy".
(
    name: "Worthy",
    template: "worthy",
    kinds: [Predicate],
    body: And([
        Supertype(Legendary),
        Not(Subtype("Villain")),
        Or([ColorIs(Red), ColorIs(White)]),
    ]),
)
